{"entryId":"3142","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:3142:1","sourceSha256":"1a197ae4ec704ca2f92d8a023c4c15c2fc6525e857d4939afb91d084c8928017","englishSha256":"da6c723f3e4bbce61fa5c58ee9d7c4cd7ade031b3f7981e46ad327f07e41b2a4","citations":[{"id":"3142:1:link-001","he":[12,24],"en":[18,29],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Niddah_46b.12"},"reference":"Niddah 46b:12","assessment":"The passage gives the name Rabbah bar Livai, spelled ליואי.","evidence":[{"reference":"Niddah 46b:12","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Niddah_46b.12"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3142:1:link-002","he":[25,96],"en":[30,128],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Pesachim_40b.3"},"reference":"Pesachim 40b:3","assessment":"The Bavli describes a shipload of wheat that sank, the challenge, and the revised sale in small amounts to Israelites before Pesah.","evidence":[{"reference":"Pesachim 40b:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Pesachim_40b.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Pesachim 40b:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Pesachim_40b.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Pesachim 40b:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Pesachim_40b.5"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3142:1:link-003","he":[98,160],"en":[143,160],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Avodah_Zarah_65b.8"},"reference":"Avodah Zarah 65b:8","assessment":"Wine poured onto a heap. The objection changes the ruling: the permitted sale is after milling and baking, out of sight of Israelites. Both cases preserve a revised permission.","evidence":[{"reference":"Avodah Zarah 65b:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Avodah_Zarah_65b.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Avodah Zarah 65b:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Avodah_Zarah_65b.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Pesachim 40b:5","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Pesachim_40b.5"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3142:1:link-004","he":[161,250],"en":[285,297],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Pesachim_110a.10"},"reference":"Pesachim 110a:10","assessment":"Rava attributes the harm to being challenged publicly. The Bavli keeps the incident in its discourse on pairs; Rashi confirms the study assembly setting.","evidence":[{"reference":"Pesachim 110a:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Pesachim_110a.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Rashi on Pesachim 110a:10:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Pesachim_110a.10.2"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1,2,3],"holds":[],"notes":[{"text":"Both soaked-wheat episodes give modified permissions after the objection. The first allows sales to Israelites in small portions and the second allows sale to gentiles after milling and baking, away from Israelites. Rava attributes the injury to the public challenge in the Bavli’s discussion of pairs.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Pesachim 110a:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Pesachim_110a.10"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Rashi on Pesachim 110a:10:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Pesachim_110a.10.2"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]}],"entryEvidence":[]}
